WEBVTT

00:00:21.710 --> 00:00:23.690
Howard!

00:00:25.510 --> 00:00:28.390
Ray... You have...

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:29.640
to live.

00:00:52.470 --> 00:00:55.120
Is that... overheating?

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:59.620
{op spot}

00:01:14.910 --> 00:01:22.790
<b>The Iceblade <b>Sorcerer
</b>Shall <b>Rule </b>the <b>World</b></b>

00:02:21.800 --> 00:02:24.990
<b>Episode 1
The Boy Who Became the World's Strongest 
Sorcerer Enters the Academy of Sorcery</b>

00:02:30.460 --> 00:02:31.880
It really is huge.

00:02:36.270 --> 00:02:38.000
Let's see...

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:39.830
Which way is the auditorium?

00:02:43.940 --> 00:02:44.900
Apologies,

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:46.680
my lady.

00:02:49.820 --> 00:02:51.960
Oh, that's all right.

00:02:51.960 --> 00:02:55.850
But I'm not sure it's a good idea to 
suddenly stop in the middle of the path.

00:02:56.240 --> 00:02:58.360
I apologize. I'm new here.

00:02:58.620 --> 00:03:02.600
What? But didn't all new students 
move onto campus two days ago?

00:03:03.560 --> 00:03:08.370
I heard there'd be just one moving in 
on the day of the entrance ceremony!

00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:10.580
One who descends from neither 
aristocrat nor sorcerer,

00:03:10.580 --> 00:03:13.210
but is born of an ordinary family.

00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:15.510
Ordinary?!

00:03:15.510 --> 00:03:16.460
Wait, that's him?

00:03:16.460 --> 00:03:18.660
First one since the school 
was founded, I heard.

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:19.710
Pretty bold for an ordinary.

00:03:19.710 --> 00:03:21.390
Did he get in on connections?

00:03:19.950 --> 00:03:23.410
I-I can't believe an 
<i>ordinary</i> just touched me...

00:03:23.940 --> 00:03:24.480
Wanda!

00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:26.180
Wanda! Keep it together!

00:03:26.180 --> 00:03:27.940
It's okay! Everything's okay!

00:03:27.940 --> 00:03:29.300
Wanda!

00:03:27.940 --> 00:03:29.930
So you're Ray White?

00:03:31.210 --> 00:03:32.150
And you are?

00:03:32.150 --> 00:03:34.180
Albert Alium.

00:03:34.510 --> 00:03:37.860
I'm Ray White. May I call you "Mr. Alium"?

00:03:38.450 --> 00:03:41.290
Only nobles are allowed 
to attend this school,

00:03:41.290 --> 00:03:44.980
or, at the very least, 
those descended from sorcerers.

00:03:44.980 --> 00:03:47.390
That's because the Arnold Academy of Sorcery

00:03:47.390 --> 00:03:50.420
has ancient and honorable 
origins as a school for nobles!

00:03:50.420 --> 00:03:52.900
Yeah, that's right! Totally right!

00:03:52.900 --> 00:03:55.670
I don't know what strings 
you pulled to get here,

00:03:55.670 --> 00:03:59.640
but this is no place for 
an ordinary like you!

00:03:59.640 --> 00:04:00.960
You tell 'im!

00:04:01.290 --> 00:04:05.800
That's unfortunate. There are many 
things I want to learn at this academy.

00:04:06.010 --> 00:04:07.220
Why, you—

00:04:09.710 --> 00:04:11.600
You worthless ordinary!

00:04:11.870 --> 00:04:12.950
Enough!

00:04:13.830 --> 00:04:14.730
Tch.

00:04:18.570 --> 00:04:20.110
Whoa! She's...

00:04:20.700 --> 00:04:22.570
From one of the top three noble families.

00:04:22.850 --> 00:04:25.360
Al, maybe you should stop...

00:04:25.620 --> 00:04:26.940
Lady Rose!

00:04:27.770 --> 00:04:28.990
She's such a treasure!

00:04:29.610 --> 00:04:30.470
Rose?

00:04:30.470 --> 00:04:31.490
Hmph!

00:04:32.210 --> 00:04:36.690
I will never accept an ordinary like you!

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:39.930
Hey! Wait up, Al!

00:04:38.730 --> 00:04:40.600
Are you all right?

00:04:40.600 --> 00:04:42.180
Yeah. Thanks.

00:04:45.480 --> 00:04:46.970
I'm Amelia Rose.

00:04:47.320 --> 00:04:48.550
Miss Rose.

00:04:49.230 --> 00:04:50.690
I'm Ray White.

00:04:50.690 --> 00:04:52.100
Feel free to call me "Ray."

00:04:52.420 --> 00:04:55.450
And you can call me "Amelia," as well.

00:04:56.460 --> 00:04:59.370
You're the first ordinary 
to attend this academy.

00:04:59.370 --> 00:05:00.690
That's a big deal.

00:05:00.970 --> 00:05:02.970
Clearly, your talents have been recognized.

00:05:02.970 --> 00:05:04.480
I couldn't be more grateful.

00:05:04.480 --> 00:05:05.840
So, Ray...

00:05:05.840 --> 00:05:06.820
What is it?

00:05:07.500 --> 00:05:10.760
If you have any problems 
at all, you can talk to me.

00:05:18.610 --> 00:05:20.330
Now, a word from our principal.

00:05:23.350 --> 00:05:24.680
Welcome, students.

00:05:25.970 --> 00:05:28.310
The Arnold Academy of Sorcery

00:05:28.310 --> 00:05:30.380
is among the finest schools in the world.

00:05:30.810 --> 00:05:32.740
All of you who stand here today

00:05:32.740 --> 00:05:35.890
have been acknowledged for 
your talents as sorcerers.

00:05:36.150 --> 00:05:39.550
But do not be prideful. 
Hard work is still a must.

00:05:39.550 --> 00:05:41.400
Spare no blood, sweat, or tears.

00:05:41.700 --> 00:05:46.780
One's skills are a product of their innate 
talent, environment, and hard work.

00:05:47.300 --> 00:05:50.060
Many sorcerers, despite remarkable 
talents and favorable environments,

00:05:50.060 --> 00:05:53.280
lose heart and let their 
abilities waste away.

00:05:53.780 --> 00:05:56.090
Thus, I tell you this:

00:05:56.770 --> 00:06:00.290
Put in the effort to become 
first-rate sorcerers.

00:06:02.630 --> 00:06:07.170
I am Abbie Garnet, the principal 
of the Arnold Academy of Sorcery.

00:06:08.280 --> 00:06:09.470
Thank you.

00:06:09.930 --> 00:06:12.720
Thank you for that speech, Principal.

00:06:13.080 --> 00:06:14.010
Next,

00:06:14.290 --> 00:06:16.680
a word from the representative 
of incoming students.

00:06:20.900 --> 00:06:24.030
I am Amelia Rose, 
representative of the incoming students.

00:06:24.340 --> 00:06:29.030
I am proud to have been accepted 
to this prestigious academy.

00:06:29.310 --> 00:06:33.490
However, this is not our destination, 
but rather our starting point.

00:06:33.800 --> 00:06:39.040
I'm sure many difficulties 
lie on the road ahead of us.

00:06:39.550 --> 00:06:42.940
But now that I am a student of this academy,

00:06:42.940 --> 00:06:45.710
I intend to face all of them head-on.

00:06:45.710 --> 00:06:48.340
As the principal said a moment ago,

00:06:48.640 --> 00:06:51.340
to continually work hard 
and master our sorcery

00:06:51.340 --> 00:06:54.660
is the mission we have undertaken.

00:06:55.870 --> 00:06:56.890
That's him?

00:06:56.890 --> 00:06:58.510
Look, it's the guy everyone's talking about.

00:06:58.510 --> 00:06:59.410
Really?

00:06:59.410 --> 00:07:00.590
Silence.

00:07:01.020 --> 00:07:02.930
This is the last student to join the class,

00:07:02.930 --> 00:07:04.600
the one I've told you about.

00:07:05.080 --> 00:07:06.350
I'm Ray White.

00:07:06.660 --> 00:07:09.900
As I'm sure many of you know, 
I come from an ordinary family.

00:07:10.810 --> 00:07:13.450
I've heard I'm the first ordinary 
at this school since it was founded,

00:07:14.120 --> 00:07:19.620
but I intend to put forth my best effort 
as a sorcerer throughout my time here.

00:07:19.620 --> 00:07:20.540
I hope we can work together.

00:07:24.130 --> 00:07:28.500
Okay, White. Sorry to just throw you 
into this, but you know the situation.

00:07:28.500 --> 00:07:31.170
You can introduce yourself to 
your classmates individually.

00:07:31.170 --> 00:07:32.550
Yes, Instructor.

00:07:33.370 --> 00:07:37.050
It's Helena Grady. You can call me Miss Gray.

00:07:37.050 --> 00:07:39.540
My apologies, Instructor Gray.

00:07:39.540 --> 00:07:41.160
Must you be so rigid?

00:07:41.160 --> 00:07:42.910
Okay, fine. Go on and sit down.

00:07:42.910 --> 00:07:43.810
Yes, ma'am.

00:07:44.790 --> 00:07:46.820
Looking forward to working with you, Ray.

00:07:46.820 --> 00:07:48.310
Same here, Amelia.

00:07:48.580 --> 00:07:50.670
Why is Lady Rose talking to him?

00:07:49.370 --> 00:07:51.370
Wait, why? Why?!

00:07:50.670 --> 00:07:52.820
One of the three top families 
is interested in him?

00:07:55.270 --> 00:07:56.820
Ordinary...

00:08:13.160 --> 00:08:14.290
White!

00:08:14.980 --> 00:08:15.840
White!

00:08:24.180 --> 00:08:26.560
Class is in session, White.

00:08:26.950 --> 00:08:28.730
You need to pay attention.

00:08:28.730 --> 00:08:30.030
I apologize.

00:08:30.370 --> 00:08:31.570
To get back on topic...

00:08:31.940 --> 00:08:34.180
We were discussing sorcerer ranks.

00:08:34.180 --> 00:08:35.450
Do you know what they are, Rose?

00:08:35.800 --> 00:08:36.580
Yes, ma'am.

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:40.750
There are five ranks established 
by the Society of Sorcery:

00:08:41.230 --> 00:08:44.410
bronze, silver, gold, platinum...

00:08:44.630 --> 00:08:47.660
and grand, the rank regarded as sacred.

00:08:48.070 --> 00:08:49.510
Correct.

00:08:49.510 --> 00:08:53.320
Only seven grand sorcerers 
exist at any one time.

00:08:53.320 --> 00:08:56.510
These seven, who have mastered 
the very essence of sorcery,

00:08:56.510 --> 00:08:59.060
are known as the seven greatest 
sorcerers in the world.

00:08:59.060 --> 00:09:02.470
They are the pinnacle of sorcery 
that all sorcerers strive to match.

00:09:02.990 --> 00:09:07.270
The very existence of the seven greatest 
sorcerers is shrouded in mystery,

00:09:07.270 --> 00:09:10.480
but a few details about them 
are known to the public.

00:09:10.770 --> 00:09:14.740
First, our very own principal, Abbie Garnet,

00:09:14.740 --> 00:09:16.490
is the Blaze Sorcerer.

00:09:16.940 --> 00:09:20.260
Next, the Spellbinding 
Sorcerer, Carol Caroline.

00:09:20.670 --> 00:09:25.930
She's the most well-known of the 
seven as a researcher of sorcery.

00:09:26.350 --> 00:09:30.650
In fact, she's just about the only one 
who really puts herself out there.

00:09:31.880 --> 00:09:36.880
And then there's the one known as 
the hero of the Far East War...

00:09:36.880 --> 00:09:38.880
The Iceblade Sorcerer.

00:09:39.090 --> 00:09:40.090
Exactly.

00:09:40.090 --> 00:09:42.890
The Iceblade Sorcerer is the one who vanished

00:09:42.890 --> 00:09:45.660
after bringing an end to the Far East War.

00:09:46.020 --> 00:09:48.130
Nothing is known about the rest of the seven.

00:09:48.130 --> 00:09:50.110
Not even their aliases.

00:09:50.580 --> 00:09:52.900
But as I said earlier,

00:09:52.900 --> 00:09:57.780
so long as you attend this academy, 
you should be aware that the destination

00:09:57.780 --> 00:10:02.530
at the end of your path is the rank of 
grand sorcerer, one of the great seven.

00:10:02.530 --> 00:10:03.940
Miss Gray.

00:10:03.940 --> 00:10:05.130
What is it, Alium?

00:10:06.200 --> 00:10:10.090
If the goal we strive for is to be 
one of the seven great sorcerers,

00:10:10.090 --> 00:10:13.400
then why is there an ordinary at this school?

00:10:13.400 --> 00:10:14.230
That's right.

00:10:13.790 --> 00:10:15.400
Why is there an ordinary?

00:10:14.230 --> 00:10:15.400
It doesn't make sense.

00:10:16.870 --> 00:10:19.900
The only students here are those 
who passed the mandated exam,

00:10:19.900 --> 00:10:24.050
as well as an in-person interview 
to be approved as students.

00:10:24.050 --> 00:10:26.550
Whether they are noble or 
ordinary means nothing.

00:10:26.550 --> 00:10:27.350
Tch.

00:10:32.110 --> 00:10:34.290
Now, it's time to practice some sorcery.

00:10:34.290 --> 00:10:36.250
You might not think it necessary anymore,

00:10:36.250 --> 00:10:39.150
but you will be starting from 
the most basic of exercises.

00:10:39.410 --> 00:10:41.060
Do not underestimate the basics.

00:10:41.060 --> 00:10:44.610
Even the seven great 
sorcerers are no exception.

00:10:44.610 --> 00:10:45.690
Now, Rose...

00:10:45.690 --> 00:10:46.160
Yes, ma'am.

00:10:46.420 --> 00:10:48.160
What is "sorcery"?

00:10:48.430 --> 00:10:52.370
Sorcery refers to the art of 
reconstructing prima materia,

00:10:52.370 --> 00:10:55.540
the primary building block 
of matter in our world.

00:10:55.870 --> 00:10:57.850
Very good. That's right.

00:10:58.540 --> 00:11:01.800
And at the very core of 
sorcery is the code theory.

00:11:02.970 --> 00:11:06.620
<i>Prima materia, encoding, material code.</i>

00:11:07.060 --> 00:11:09.590
First, you encode prima materia,

00:11:09.590 --> 00:11:11.430
or in other words, turn it into code.

00:11:11.430 --> 00:11:14.920
At this stage, there is still excess data.

00:11:14.920 --> 00:11:16.100
So...

00:11:16.100 --> 00:11:20.190
<i>Material code, decoding, material code.</i>

00:11:20.190 --> 00:11:21.960
You remove the excess by decoding,

00:11:21.960 --> 00:11:26.050
put the data back in order, 
and move to the processing stage.

00:11:26.490 --> 00:11:28.780
<i>Material code, processing.</i>

00:11:29.130 --> 00:11:32.750
Here, you can add or remove more data.

00:11:32.750 --> 00:11:34.930
Finally, you manifest it.

00:11:34.930 --> 00:11:37.250
<i>Embodiment, material.</i>

00:11:39.900 --> 00:11:41.810
These are the fundamentals of sorcery.

00:11:43.210 --> 00:11:45.670
Additionally, anything you have made...

00:11:46.940 --> 00:11:49.240
you can also erase.

00:11:49.990 --> 00:11:54.560
Sorcery is a theoretical phenomenon derived 
from the understanding of technique.

00:11:54.990 --> 00:11:58.290
Any questions about what 
I've explained thus far?

00:11:58.290 --> 00:11:59.480
I have one, ma'am.

00:11:59.770 --> 00:12:01.560
You do, Rose? Very well.

00:12:02.090 --> 00:12:06.150
Are there any limits on the things 
reconstructed by prima materia?

00:12:06.470 --> 00:12:09.570
No, strictly speaking, there are no limits.

00:12:09.570 --> 00:12:12.160
It all depends on the 
sorcerer's own capability.

00:12:12.840 --> 00:12:17.420
Sorcery is, primarily, the art 
of creating matter or phenomena.

00:12:17.870 --> 00:12:20.540
Matter can be separated into four categories.

00:12:22.000 --> 00:12:23.150
Solids.

00:12:25.590 --> 00:12:26.760
Liquids.

00:12:28.340 --> 00:12:29.430
Gases.

00:12:30.750 --> 00:12:33.220
And finally, plasma.

00:12:33.620 --> 00:12:36.940
Anything else is classified as a phenomenon.

00:12:40.250 --> 00:12:41.600
Anyone else?

00:12:41.600 --> 00:12:42.950
U-Um...

00:12:43.690 --> 00:12:46.760
When you erased the ice roses earlier,

00:12:46.760 --> 00:12:49.320
did you use anti-material code?

00:12:49.320 --> 00:12:55.330
No. There is no sorcerer who 
uses anti-material code.

00:12:55.820 --> 00:12:59.580
Ainsworth's twofold code theory 
is doctorate-level material.

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:01.790
Students don't need to understand it yet.

00:13:03.590 --> 00:13:05.300
Now for some exercises.

00:13:09.400 --> 00:13:11.760
<i>Prima materia, encoding.</i>

00:13:11.760 --> 00:13:13.120
<i>Material code.</i>

00:13:13.120 --> 00:13:15.450
<i>Material code, decoding.</i>

00:13:13.850 --> 00:13:16.410
<i>Material code, processing.</i>

00:13:16.950 --> 00:13:18.940
<i>Embodiment, material.</i>

00:13:22.070 --> 00:13:25.540
I knew you could do it, 
Lady Rose! Magnificent!

00:13:24.820 --> 00:13:26.770
Th-Thanks...

00:13:25.540 --> 00:13:28.660
Leave it to a lady of one 
of the highest noble families.

00:13:26.770 --> 00:13:30.570
I love it so, so, so, so, so, so much!

00:13:28.300 --> 00:13:30.090
Uh, yeah...

00:13:28.660 --> 00:13:30.570
On the other hand...

00:13:33.410 --> 00:13:35.660
Hmm... I see.

00:13:35.960 --> 00:13:37.590
What was that supposed to be?

00:13:37.590 --> 00:13:39.410
That was a child's sorcery.

00:13:39.410 --> 00:13:41.710
But didn't the teacher 
say he passed the exam?

00:13:41.710 --> 00:13:43.530
What's his deal, anyway?

00:13:43.530 --> 00:13:45.130
He's totally useless.

00:13:47.720 --> 00:13:49.350
Ordinary...

00:13:49.350 --> 00:13:51.090
Whoa... Al?!

00:13:51.620 --> 00:13:53.800
<i>As a member of the Alium household,</i>

00:13:53.800 --> 00:13:59.170
<i>I refuse to acknowledge the existence 
of a talentless Withered Wizard!</i>

00:14:02.320 --> 00:14:05.210
This is definitely a 
historical school building.

00:14:05.210 --> 00:14:07.150
Its construction is flawless.

00:14:12.730 --> 00:14:13.820
Looking for Ainsworth?

00:14:13.820 --> 00:14:14.920
Huh?! Ah...

00:14:14.920 --> 00:14:17.530
You asked about it in class earlier.

00:14:17.530 --> 00:14:19.720
Oh... Um, I...

00:14:19.720 --> 00:14:22.380
Sorry for asking out of nowhere. 
I'm Ray White.

00:14:22.380 --> 00:14:23.810
Oh... um...

00:14:23.810 --> 00:14:25.850
I'm Elisa Griffith.

00:14:25.850 --> 00:14:27.930
Nice to meet you, Miss Griffith.

00:14:27.930 --> 00:14:29.680
You can call me "Ray."

00:14:29.680 --> 00:14:32.780
Oh... And you can call me "Elisa."

00:14:33.100 --> 00:14:35.650
Once more, nice to meet you, Elisa.

00:14:35.650 --> 00:14:36.880
Same to you.

00:14:38.480 --> 00:14:40.890
Dr. Ainsworth is my role model.

00:14:41.590 --> 00:14:44.130
So that's why you asked about 
the twofold code theory.

00:14:44.130 --> 00:14:47.440
Yeah. I want to be just like her.

00:14:47.440 --> 00:14:51.250
That's amazing. She's a top-ranking 
researcher of sorcery.

00:14:52.020 --> 00:14:54.590
Well, it's just a dream.

00:14:55.250 --> 00:14:58.490
Do you like Dr. Ainsworth, too?

00:14:58.490 --> 00:15:01.970
Yeah. I love her from the bottom of my heart.

00:15:01.970 --> 00:15:06.600
Really?! Wow! I've never met 
any other Ainsers my age!

00:15:06.840 --> 00:15:08.580
Ainsers?

00:15:08.580 --> 00:15:09.380
Oh...

00:15:10.000 --> 00:15:13.470
That means... fans of Dr. Ainsworth.

00:15:13.470 --> 00:15:16.400
Never heard that before. 
There's actually a word for them, huh?

00:15:16.960 --> 00:15:20.410
I'm sorry for getting so carried away.

00:15:20.410 --> 00:15:22.900
I don't mind. Why, though?

00:15:22.900 --> 00:15:23.660
Why what?

00:15:24.340 --> 00:15:26.660
You have such beautiful hair.

00:15:26.660 --> 00:15:27.390
Huh?!

00:15:29.200 --> 00:15:29.830
Elisa...

00:15:31.500 --> 00:15:32.890
is there some reason?

00:15:34.460 --> 00:15:37.370
Well... don't you think my ears are weird?

00:15:37.370 --> 00:15:38.430
They're not weird.

00:15:39.190 --> 00:15:40.430
They're lovely.

00:15:41.070 --> 00:15:44.010
So you're an elf... no, a half-elf, right?

00:15:44.530 --> 00:15:46.520
My mother is an elf.

00:15:46.750 --> 00:15:49.710
I've been made fun of all my 
life because of these ears.

00:15:49.710 --> 00:15:51.670
I think you're beautiful, Elisa.

00:15:52.130 --> 00:15:52.520
Huh?!

00:15:53.270 --> 00:15:55.980
So what need is there to hide them?

00:15:58.260 --> 00:16:02.630
I-I'm glad you think so, I guess.

00:16:03.630 --> 00:16:06.130
You seem very mature, Ray.

00:16:06.130 --> 00:16:07.040
Do I?

00:16:07.040 --> 00:16:10.040
Yeah. You don't look like you're my age.

00:16:10.620 --> 00:16:14.960
Jeez, kid, you act way too old for your age.

00:16:15.310 --> 00:16:16.550
You're too mature!

00:16:17.520 --> 00:16:20.180
I guess I do get that a lot.

00:16:20.530 --> 00:16:21.790
I thought so.

00:16:23.910 --> 00:16:26.210
Thank you for talking to me today, Ray.

00:16:26.210 --> 00:16:29.020
Same to you. I look forward to 
spending more time together.

00:16:29.290 --> 00:16:31.760
Um... See you tomorrow.

00:16:31.760 --> 00:16:32.470
Yeah.

00:16:37.050 --> 00:16:38.110
Pardon me.

00:16:38.110 --> 00:16:40.650
I've been waiting for you, Ray White.

00:16:42.830 --> 00:16:44.580
You're Evi Armstrong?

00:16:45.030 --> 00:16:47.170
Call me "Evi," Ray.

00:16:47.530 --> 00:16:50.380
Oh? I appreciate the invitation.

00:16:50.380 --> 00:16:52.950
I'm not like those noble kids.

00:16:52.950 --> 00:16:55.290
I don't care if you're an ordinary.

00:16:55.750 --> 00:16:58.300
There's only one thing I believe in.

00:17:03.040 --> 00:17:05.800
I knew it! Just like I thought!

00:17:05.800 --> 00:17:08.100
Evi, you're...

00:17:10.690 --> 00:17:12.190
You've got some nice bulk.

00:17:12.900 --> 00:17:14.240
Same to you.

00:17:16.030 --> 00:17:17.930
You're welcome here, Ray!

00:17:17.930 --> 00:17:19.620
Thanks! Nice to meet you!

00:17:30.230 --> 00:17:31.090
Huh?

00:17:33.100 --> 00:17:34.690
Sorry about that.

00:17:34.690 --> 00:17:36.760
I wasn't expecting anyone to be here.

00:17:36.760 --> 00:17:38.240
It's all right.

00:17:38.550 --> 00:17:41.020
Running so early in the 
morning is very impressive.

00:17:41.020 --> 00:17:43.260
Are you an incoming student?

00:17:43.260 --> 00:17:46.100
Yes. My name is Ray White.

00:17:46.100 --> 00:17:47.760
Oh! You're Ray White?

00:17:47.760 --> 00:17:49.260
You know of me?

00:17:49.260 --> 00:17:53.480
The academy's first ordinary. 
You're very famous.

00:17:53.480 --> 00:17:54.770
I'm honored.

00:17:54.980 --> 00:17:58.720
My name is Rebecca Bradley. I'm a third-year.

00:17:58.720 --> 00:18:00.780
Feel free to call me "Rebecca."

00:18:01.050 --> 00:18:03.280
I'll do that, Rebecca.

00:18:03.510 --> 00:18:05.110
Good, Ray.

00:18:06.820 --> 00:18:10.540
Bradley? That's one of the 
top three noble families!

00:18:10.540 --> 00:18:11.790
Top three noble families?

00:18:12.010 --> 00:18:13.810
You really don't know?

00:18:13.810 --> 00:18:16.090
Well, I grew up in the countryside.

00:18:16.090 --> 00:18:17.850
I don't know much about the nobility.

00:18:18.320 --> 00:18:21.210
Rose, Bradley, and Olgren.

00:18:21.780 --> 00:18:25.320
Those three families are as 
powerful as the royal family,

00:18:25.320 --> 00:18:28.160
with just as much influence over politics,

00:18:28.160 --> 00:18:29.900
the economy, and everything 
else in this country.

00:18:30.220 --> 00:18:32.140
That's who the top three noble families are.

00:18:32.140 --> 00:18:33.980
So Amelia is...

00:18:33.980 --> 00:18:37.070
The eldest daughter of the Rose family, 
the highest of the three.

00:18:37.070 --> 00:18:41.770
She's got spotless integrity, high morals, 
and first-rate sorcerer skills.

00:18:41.770 --> 00:18:44.780
She's a genuine, born-and-bred lady.

00:18:47.340 --> 00:18:49.200
Evi, you can go on ahead.

00:18:49.200 --> 00:18:50.010
Huh?

00:18:50.010 --> 00:18:51.830
The instructor wanted to see me.

00:18:51.830 --> 00:18:55.100
Okay. Remember, first period 
is practical swordsmanship.

00:18:55.100 --> 00:18:56.850
We'll have to change, so get there early.

00:18:56.850 --> 00:18:57.580
Right.

00:19:00.130 --> 00:19:01.960
Whoa!

00:19:04.350 --> 00:19:05.920
Are you all right?

00:19:08.090 --> 00:19:10.720
Hey! Watch where you're going!

00:19:10.720 --> 00:19:14.100
My apologies. I was just 
walking like normal, though...

00:19:14.100 --> 00:19:16.820
Well, I was running because 
I was kind of in a hurry!

00:19:16.820 --> 00:19:18.540
So you should have moved aside!

00:19:18.540 --> 00:19:22.440
Uh-huh... That's awfully 
unreasonable, but I do apologize.

00:19:22.950 --> 00:19:25.630
You're weird. Wait...

00:19:25.630 --> 00:19:27.330
Aren't you that ordinary?!

00:19:27.330 --> 00:19:29.200
I'm Ray White. Nice to meet you,

00:19:29.510 --> 00:19:31.610
my charming, pigtailed lady.

00:19:32.390 --> 00:19:35.110
Well, you certainly know just where to look!

00:19:35.110 --> 00:19:37.980
You actually recognized the 
greatness of these pigtails!

00:19:37.980 --> 00:19:38.830
Really?

00:19:39.740 --> 00:19:41.990
I am the first and the last,

00:19:41.990 --> 00:19:44.380
the girl of transcendent, raging cuteness...

00:19:44.590 --> 00:19:48.930
The girl who loves and 
is loved by pigtails...

00:19:48.930 --> 00:19:53.010
I am Claris Cleve...

00:19:53.010 --> 00:19:54.950
land!

00:19:56.800 --> 00:19:58.670
Wow, how nice.

00:19:59.060 --> 00:20:01.590
I'm not familiar with 
the "Cleve Land" family,

00:20:01.590 --> 00:20:03.400
but I hope we can get along.

00:20:03.400 --> 00:20:06.300
What?! You don't know the Clevelands?

00:20:06.300 --> 00:20:10.150
I'm sorry. I grew up in the countryside, 
so I don't know much about the nobility.

00:20:10.380 --> 00:20:13.660
I see. Well, that's fine... yeah.

00:20:13.890 --> 00:20:16.630
It's a pretty well-known family, though...

00:20:16.630 --> 00:20:18.950
I see... You don't know us, huh?

00:20:18.950 --> 00:20:21.660
But I'm sure it's a beautiful family.

00:20:21.660 --> 00:20:23.670
That's clear just from looking at you.

00:20:24.180 --> 00:20:25.090
You can tell?!

00:20:25.530 --> 00:20:27.970
Oh, very well, then!

00:20:27.970 --> 00:20:31.410
I'll grant you special permission 
to call me "Claris," Ray!

00:20:31.410 --> 00:20:34.630
I appreciate that. 
I hope we'll get along, Claris.

00:20:35.350 --> 00:20:37.750
I suppose I'll let you get along with me!

00:20:38.550 --> 00:20:40.890
Anyway, weren't you in a hurry?

00:20:40.890 --> 00:20:42.030
Oh, crap!

00:20:42.030 --> 00:20:44.070
Well, bye! See you later!

00:20:44.070 --> 00:20:44.610
Okay.

00:20:49.090 --> 00:20:50.890
Welcome, Ray.

00:20:51.590 --> 00:20:53.610
It's good to see you again, Colonel.

00:20:53.610 --> 00:20:57.210
None of that, now. You and I have 
both retired from the service.

00:20:57.210 --> 00:20:59.120
What shall I call you, then?

00:20:59.620 --> 00:21:00.710
Just "Abbie."

00:21:00.710 --> 00:21:02.900
Understood, Abbie.

00:21:05.360 --> 00:21:06.770
You haven't changed.

00:21:06.770 --> 00:21:09.510
That part of you is so much like him.

00:21:10.690 --> 00:21:13.530
It brings back memories, doesn't it, Abbie?

00:21:13.530 --> 00:21:14.450
Uh, hey...

00:21:15.540 --> 00:21:18.590
Albert Alium and Ray White.

00:21:19.530 --> 00:21:21.640
This is no more than a mock battle.

00:21:21.640 --> 00:21:23.850
If it looks like it's getting 
dangerous, I'll stop you.

00:21:24.220 --> 00:21:26.020
Look, it's the Withered.

00:21:25.110 --> 00:21:27.100
Hah, the Withered!

00:21:26.310 --> 00:21:28.020
Who the heck said he was good, anyway?

00:21:28.280 --> 00:21:29.430
Withered?

00:21:30.270 --> 00:21:32.170
They call him the "Withered Wizard."

00:21:32.170 --> 00:21:32.860
Huh?

00:21:32.860 --> 00:21:35.520
I'm Ray's bosom buddy, Evi.

00:21:35.520 --> 00:21:38.830
Oh, well, hello... But what does that mean?

00:21:38.830 --> 00:21:40.600
It's wordplay.

00:21:40.600 --> 00:21:42.500
"Withered" and "Wizard"...

00:21:42.960 --> 00:21:45.090
They're practically the same word.

00:21:45.090 --> 00:21:46.880
Oh, I get it.

00:21:46.880 --> 00:21:48.210
<i>Ray...</i>

00:21:49.010 --> 00:21:50.790
Okay, are you both ready?

00:21:50.790 --> 00:21:53.810
<i>Someone who can't even use sorcery...</i>

00:21:53.810 --> 00:21:54.640
Begin!

00:21:54.640 --> 00:21:57.050
...has no right to stand 
on the same level as me!

00:22:03.230 --> 00:22:04.250
No way!

00:22:04.250 --> 00:22:05.490
Not bad, man!

00:22:05.490 --> 00:22:06.480
Impossible!

00:22:06.710 --> 00:22:07.520
Ray!

00:22:08.160 --> 00:22:10.850
That doesn't have too much influence on me.

00:22:11.910 --> 00:22:14.070
You... You...

00:22:14.620 --> 00:22:17.320
You damned Withered!

00:22:25.010 --> 00:22:25.890
No way...

00:22:25.890 --> 00:22:27.030
For real?

00:22:29.250 --> 00:22:32.550
I'm glad to see you enjoying 
your student life,

00:22:34.590 --> 00:22:35.950
Ray White...

00:22:36.940 --> 00:22:38.930
the Iceblade Sorcerer.

00:23:50.000 --> 00:23:54.470
Students! This is the preview for 
<i>The Iceblade Sorcerer Shall Rule the World</i>!

00:23:50.000 --> 00:23:54.990
<b>The Iceblade <b>Sorcerer
</b>Shall <b>Rule </b>the <b>World</b></b>

00:23:50.000 --> 00:23:54.990
<b>~ Next Episode Preview ~</b>

00:23:54.990 --> 00:23:56.910
Having quietly made up his mind,

00:23:56.910 --> 00:23:59.290
Ray heads to the place that's a sanctuary
 for fierce, impassioned muscle men,

00:23:59.290 --> 00:24:02.460
and a garden for pure, elegant young ladies.

00:24:02.460 --> 00:24:06.100
"The Boy Who Became the World's Strongest 
Sorcerer Begins His Practical Exercises."

00:24:05.500 --> 00:24:10.250
<b>Episode 2
The Boy Who Became the World's Strongest 
Sorcerer Begins His Practical Exercises</b>

00:24:06.680 --> 00:24:09.260
Abbie Garnet, signing off!
